deployed: 2026-05-12T03:00:00Z · v1.0.63 (Token list prices fixed — three coordinated changes.

1. _tokRenderList now triggers _tokFetchLive for EVERY visible row, staggered 80ms apart so the rate-limit hit spreads across Binance/Birdeye instead of a single bulk burst. Previously the fetch only fired for the selected token (in _tokRenderProfile), so list rows like BNB/DOGE/BONK/JTO/JUP that the player never selected stayed at "—" forever even though they had Binance pairs ready to populate.

2. _tokSnapshot.px logic changed: never synth-fake a price for tokens we KNOW have a real source. New _hasBird check joins _hasBin + _hasPyth in the "has a real source → show '—' while loading, never synth" branch. Old behavior: tokens with no Binance pair fell through to rng()*1000+0.001, which is how FART rendered at $717.84.

3. PUMP + FART mints removed from TOK_BIRDEYE_MINT. The placeholders I shipped in v1.0.52 were guesses that 404'd on Birdeye. Without the bad mints, Birdeye stops eating retries on them. Restore when canonical PUMP/FART mainnet mints are confirmed.

Net effect: open Token Terminal, all visible rows populate within ~2 seconds (80ms × 22 tokens staggered). Tokens with no real source show "—" cleanly, no more $717 fake prices.)
